---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../consts';
import OperatorDetails from '../components/OperatorDetails.astro';
---

<Base title={`Support — ${SITE.name}`} description="Setup help and troubleshooting for CamLock.">
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Help</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. Include your phone
        model, Android version, app version and what happened. Please omit children’s photos,
        face templates, ID documents and unredacted history.
      </p>

      <h2>Protection keeps stopping on its own</h2>
      <p>
        Some manufacturers kill background services aggressively. In CamLock, open Settings >
        Permissions and access, tap Open on the Battery row, pick CamLock in Android's list and turn
        optimisation off. On Samsung and Xiaomi, also allow CamLock to run unrestricted in its app
        battery settings. CamLock can report an unexpected stop when it next runs. Alert delivery depends on Android
        and notification access; it cannot send an immediate alert while force-stopped.
      </p>

      <h2>My child is not recognised</h2>
      <p>
        Add more face samples from a second angle and in different light: open the child, then
        "Add more face samples". If that does not help, move the sensitivity preset to lenient.
      </p>

      <h2>The phone locks for the wrong person</h2>
      <p>
        Similar faces, lighting and camera angle can cause mistaken matches. Move the sensitivity preset to
        strict, and re-enrol the affected child with clear, well-lit samples.
      </p>

      <h2>It does not lock after a reboot</h2>
      <p>
        Android does not allow a camera service to start in the background. CamLock posts a
        reminder after a reboot. Tap it and authenticate with your biometric; protection can restart
        once the required permissions and access are ready.
      </p>

      <h2>I cannot get into the app</h2>
      <p>
        CamLock requires a strong biometric, with no PIN fallback. If your fingerprint is not
        recognised, or none is enrolled, enrol one in Android Settings and reopen the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Delete app data and exported files</h2>
      <p>
        Settings has "Delete all data" to stop protection and clear saved profiles, face templates,
        history and settings when deletion finishes successfully. Uninstalling removes app-private
        data. Removing just one child keeps older history; use "Delete history" to clear it.
        Exported CSVs, copies in cloud storage, original gallery photos and support emails remain
        separate. Delete those at their destination, or contact us about correspondence we hold.
      </p>

      <h2>History exports</h2>
      <p>
        Android's file picker lets you choose where a CSV is saved, including available cloud
        providers. The file can contain child names and activity details and is not encrypted by
        CamLock. Keep it private and share only the rows needed for your purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact and complaints</h2>
      <OperatorDetails />
      <p>
        Send support requests, privacy enquiries or written complaints to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
        Describe the issue and the outcome you are requesting. See the{' '}
        <a href={url('/privacy')}>privacy policy</a> for how correspondence is handled.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 44rem; }
  .prose h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem); letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.05; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin-top: 2.25rem; }
  .prose p { color: var(--muted); }
  .prose .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; }
</style>
